	"web_text": null,
	"didactic_label": "This model of a traditional ceremonial house (kashim) with carved figures may have been made as a commemorative model or a teaching tool. The faces of the three drummers are lined with age and experience. At the end of the nineteenth century it was customary for male dancers to appear stripped to the waist, wearing only pants made of Siberian reindeer skins. Four of the dancers on display wear pants made of cormorant feathers, whose color and texture resemble deer skin.",
	"exhibition_history_text": null,
	"exhibition_history_lines": [],
	"bibliography_text": null,
