		"parsed": false
	},
	"label_text": null,
	"publication_text": "The dance scene in this particular tableau (kasginguaq) depicts the northern-style dance known as puallak in Yup’ik. The vigorous and energetic style of dance takes place inside a qasgi, or men’s house. (Olcott, Hillary C. et. al., Yua, Spirit of the Arctic: Highlights from the Thomas G. Fowler Collection (San Francisco: Fine Arts Museums of San Francisco, 2020), pp. 107-109, fig. 11, no. 52, entry by Chuna McIntyre, consulting curator, Thomas G. Fowler Collection.)",
